Subject: [PATCH] mac80211: derive PKG_BUILD_ID from SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH

Both mac80211 packages used a timestamp as the module build-id seed:

    PKG_BUILD_ID:=$(shell date | $(MKHASH) md5)

The value is passed to the linker through include/kernel.mk:120
(LDFLAGS_MODULE=--build-id=0x$(PKG_BUILD_ID)) and lands as the 16-byte
.note.gnu.build-id of every module built by the package.  Because `date`
returns wall-clock time at parse time, two clean builds of the same tree
produce different module bytes (measured: 9 ipks, 16 bytes each at file
offset 81-96; see docs/G35C_REPRODUCIBILITY.md section 3.4).

Seed it from SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH instead, which include/toplevel.mk already
exports as a fixed value (scripts/get_source_date_epoch.sh).  PKG_SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
is kept as a fallback for the (unlikely) case of parsing without TOPDIR.
If both are empty the seed is still constant, so the build-id remains
reproducible.

This changes binary contents (only the build-id note) once; it does not
change any compiled code, vermagic, or package metadata.

Observed during the G3.5 reproducibility verification, 2026-10-21.

---
--- a/package/kernel/mac80211/Makefile
+++ b/package/kernel/mac80211/Makefile
@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@
 PKG_BUILD_PARALLEL:=1

 MKHASH ?= $(STAGING_DIR_HOST)/bin/mkhash
-PKG_BUILD_ID:=$(shell date | $(MKHASH) md5)
+PKG_BUILD_ID:=$(shell echo $(if $(SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH),$(SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH),$(PKG_SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH)) | $(MKHASH) md5)
 PKG_MAINTAINER:=Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>

 PKG_DRIVERS = \
--- a/qca/feeds/wlan-open/mac80211/Makefile
+++ b/qca/feeds/wlan-open/mac80211/Makefile
@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@
 PKG_BUILD_PARALLEL:=1

 MKHASH ?= $(STAGING_DIR_HOST)/bin/mkhash
-PKG_BUILD_ID:=$(shell date | $(MKHASH) md5)
+PKG_BUILD_ID:=$(shell echo $(if $(SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH),$(SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH),$(PKG_SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH)) | $(MKHASH) md5)

 ifeq (y, $(filter y, $(CONFIG_TARGET_echo) $(CONFIG_TARGET_sdx85)))
 	SRCPREFIX:=
